  <p>Two rows need their caveats read. The 990 pixel Tmall sign width comes from three sources that separate Tmall from Taobao, and none of them is newer than 2023, so it may not describe the current builder. And the carousel height has four different answers, so it is the row most likely to be quoted to you with a confidence the record does not support.</p>

  <h2>Do Tmall store modules differ between mobile and PC?</h2>

  <p>Yes, and the mobile side is where this page has to be most careful, because it is where the published sizes agree least.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">The mobile homepage width depends on when the source was written. The oldest material describes a 640 pixel grid. Pages from 2021 to 2024 give 750 pixels, which is still the most repeated figure. A 2023 Tmall table and 2026 product modules give 1200. One page dated May 2026 quotes a change notice asking for image modules 1440 pixels wide and 144 to 2400 pixels tall, and prints 1400 in its own table. That figure is found once, so treat it as contested, not as the new rule.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: 6 independent Chinese-language domains giving a mobile width, grouped by publication date before counting, pages dated about 2020 to May 2026, collected 10 September 2026. Modal value by count is 750, contested and split by age. Not a primary reading.</p>

  <p>This is the row where counting alone gives the wrong answer. The most repeated figure, 750, is also among the older ones. The newest figures are wider and rest on fewer pages, including one that contradicts its own table.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
