  <p>Plan the refresh from that list, build mobile modules wide, and take each size from the store builder on the day of production rather than from any page, this one included.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/resources/insights/tmall-product-image-requirements">Tmall product image requirements article</a> covers the listing images inside the store, the <a href="/resources/insights/china-ecommerce-content-pack">article on what a China ecommerce content pack contains</a> covers the full deliverable list for a SKU, and the <a href="/solutions/brands">brands solutions page</a> covers running a flagship across campaigns.</p>

  <p>Reviewed 10 September 2026. Confirm every figure in your own seller backend before building a batch to it.</p>

  <h2>Questions about Tmall store decoration</h2>

  <h3>What size is a Tmall store banner?</h3>

  <p>On desktop the most published full-screen carousel is 1920 pixels wide, agreed by every source giving a width, with height contested between 400 and 800 pixels and 600 most common. The desktop sign band is 150 pixels tall. These are counted published values rather than figures read from Tmall, so confirm them in the store builder.</p>

  <h3>Do Tmall store modules differ between mobile and PC?</h3>

  <p>Yes. Desktop sizes mostly agree across sources. Mobile widths split by publication date: 640 pixels on the oldest material, 750 on pages from 2021 to 2024, 1200 on newer pages, and 1440 found once in 2026. Building mobile modules at the widest published width and exporting down avoids depending on which figure is current.</p>

  <h3>How many assets does a Tmall store refresh need?</h3>

  <p>No source publishes a count, because it depends on how many floors and modules a store runs. A refresh touches the store sign and background, navigation, carousel banners and homepage image modules on both desktop and mobile, plus any campaign redress. Take each size from the store builder on the day of production.</p>

  <h3>How does a Singles Day store skin differ from an always-on store?</h3>

  <p>No published source gives separate dimensions for a 618 or Singles Day skin. Pages discussing campaign stores cover color, mood and mascots, not module sizes, so a skin is, on the public record, the same modules redressed. The store live tab has no published size at all, so check both directly in the store builder.</p>
